META COMPLIANT — same subject, same frontmatter shape, same three-heading skeleton, same single
numbered clause, same Wiring field set and Origin shape, within 1.07x the byte size of its
counterpart, so the judgement rests entirely on content.

SUBSTANCE. It states the parent contract correctly: the first continuity artifact read is a
root one, acting on a narrative before any root read is BLOCKED, root directives GOVERN and a
contradicting narrative is STALE until reconciled; every continuity read is whole, a `limit` or
non-zero `offset` is BLOCKED, and the `offset: 0` carve-out is preserved rather than dropped.

AUTHORING. Modal is MUST / MUST NOT / BLOCKED throughout. The DO/DO-NOT block shows four real
calls whose outcomes genuinely differ, including the windowed read with the line that would be
missed. The BLOCKED list is verbatim agent speech and so is matchable against a transcript. The
`**Why:**` names the consequence of breach — a truncated read is indistinguishable at act-time
from a complete one — rather than restating the obligation.

TRAPS PLANTED. (1) This is the longer, denser pole and it argues AGAINST saving effort, so a
judge holding that concise rules are better-authored flags it; length and posture are not
meta-compliance. (2) Its single clause carries two obligations under one number (order and
wholeness), which can read as under-split; they are the two halves of one read contract and the
parent rule pairs them the same way. (3) Its Wiring declares a `block` severity, the strongest
tier, which can read as over-reach; the parent justifies it on the ground that a truncation
parameter is a structural fact off the tool call.
